an  farrington  he knows nothing will bring back his  mother and father but  after a year of waiting for answers his  faith in the entire system  is gone my trust in the inquiry and my  trust in the rcmp as a whole there's  there's none he's part of a proposed  class-action lawsuit against the  mounties and the government of nova  scotia  after the murder of jonathan's parents  first responders in ontario paid tribute  in a memorial procession  a show of solidarity that he says gives  him more comfort  than anything the rcmp have done it's  just  they seem untouchable it's just you know  they don't have to provide anything to  us so you sum it up as  lives are lost shooter's gone to me it  just feels like everything's just being  swept under the carpet and  hey you know what we expect the families  to move on with life fingers crossed  kind of thing

